        "source": "d2_memory_dispatch.py:MemoryDispatch.submit",
        "assessment": "Exact bounded bytes and bounded primitive synthetic peer labels are copied before admission. Queue operations and unique ticket assignment are serialized under the same RLock. Queue-full rejects without eviction or consuming a ticket. Enqueue does not authenticate the peer or accept a broker operation."
      },
      {
        "source": "d2_memory_dispatch.py:MemoryDispatch.dispatch_next/_publish",
        "assessment": "The head request is evaluated against the current immutable model at dequeue, under the publication/removal lock. The unchanged model checks synthetic peer instance and generation before cached request handling. Duplicate stop yields no additional model revision or false cleanup claim. No callback, caller snapshot or external executor is accepted."
      },
      {
        "source": "d2_memory_dispatch.py:MemoryDispatch.close/dispatch_next/submit",
        "assessment": "Explicit close, ticket exhaustion and unexpected calculation Exception close admission and publish recovery-unknown through the unchanged model. Queue/head and terminal history remain retained; exceptions propagate rather than fabricate stop completion. Closed fixtures cannot rearm; retained entries can be drained for model refusals. This has no OS effect or persistent fence."
      },
      {
        "source": "test_d2_memory_dispatch.py",
        "assessment": "The new suite uses in-process threads/events, a synthetic calculation patch and a private ticket-boundary fixture. It checks FIFO, concurrent tickets/drain publication, delayed calculation ordering, old-G/old-peer dispatch, duplicate stop, bounded admission, unknown latching and BLOCKED exports. Imported old test modules provide message/peer/proof helpers; their test cases are not selected by the new module invocation."
      }
    ],
    "retained_limitations": [
      "Queue-full may reject stop; no priority or independent stop path exists.",
